# fixtures/hex/fragments/runtime/os-ids.hex: the X-F8 runtime structures in the forms store A (a Windows NTFS
# volume) does not hold. Decode: five OsFileId (57 B each, [F11 §12.1]), then five VolumeCaps (16 B each,
# [F11 §12.3]), then five FsTime (9 B each, [F11 §12.2]). Volume keys are BLAKE3-128 of synthetic labels; the
# Linux id's hgen is the first 8 bytes of BLAKE3-256 over u32le(handle_type) and a synthetic 8-byte f_handle.

# OsFileId
# kind 0: none (no identity: every field zero): OsFileId kind 0 `none` (57 B, [F11 §12.1])
  00*57                                     # kind 0: every field zero
# kind 1 ntfs128: FILE_ID_128 of the file and of its parent directory: OsFileId kind 1 `ntfs128` (57 B, [F11 §12.1])
  01                                        # kind
